# PCA-Based Neural Network Emulator for Cosmological Power Spectra

This project implements a **Principal Component Analysis (PCA)-based Neural Network (NN) approach** for emulating two-point correlation functions.

We discuss how to apply this method to emulate **CMB angular power spectra** and **matter power spectra**. We then use the trained emulator to sample cosmological parameters using the **Planck likelihood code**, specifically the lighter version in which nuisance parameters have been marginalized over.

## Installation Guide

To install the required packages, **please pay careful attention to the package versions**.

Run the commands provided in the `installation_guide.sh` file from the terminal.

Before running the installation commands, you should install **Anaconda** on your computer:

[Download Anaconda](https://www.anaconda.com/download)

After installing Anaconda, follow the instructions in `installation_guide.sh` to create and configure the required environment.

